  "body": "Split from #2201 by the maintainer's order in chat, 2026-11-16 (\"these selection gpu/cpu issues needs to be P1 - they tank the application\"). #2201 keeps the hover and highlight path, which mkinney's claim holds. This issue is the cost of the selected chains.\n\nWhat happens: an operation has chains in its geometry selection. Each frame then does work in proportion to the selected chains. The app is not usable.\n\nEvidence, project `testdata/models/fig8.camproj`, 2D Adaptive, Geometry tab, \"Click selects: Edges\":\n\n| Build | Selection | Frame | scene | ui |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| PR #2215 `6cf7cf9` | none | 145 to 170 ms | 77 to 83 ms | 65 to 72 ms |\n| PR #2215 `6cf7cf9` | an edge all around the part | 1090 to 1300 ms | 650 to 725 ms | 440 to 485 ms |\n| `134790d0` (no edge join) | 11 open chains, \"11 open runs stitched into 2 rings\" | about 1600 ms | - | - |\n\nThe full logs are on #2209 and #2201. The cost is constant from frame to frame. Thus the work runs again in each frame and is not a one-time calculation at the click.\n\nCandidates:\n\n1. The ring stitch of the selected runs (\"N open runs stitched into M rings\").\n2. The chain rows of the Geometry tab (length, \"k of n\", ring number).\n3. The geometry of the selection overlay in the viewport.\n\nExpected: the app calculates these one time when the selection or the model changes. A frame without a change reads the stored result.\n\nLimits:\n\n- Do not change the hover path or the highlighter. That is #2201.\n- Do not change which chains a pick gives, the stitch result, or the geometry that an operation cuts along. The posted G-code stays the same.\n\nDone means:\n\n- A test counts the calculations: frames without a selection change do no stitch and no chain measurement.\n- With an edge selected all around the part on `fig8.step`, the `scene` and `ui` phases are not slower than with no selection, within the measurement noise.\n- A release test build is at `.claude/tmp/test-builds/` for the maintainer.\n",
